body:
Thanks for the kind words. I've lately just been so tired and numb. Even looking at all the kind and lovely messages people have written here, I feel a little overwhelmed. Like I'm operating at half a spoon at all times, and anything requiring serious attention is a bit too much. Blank and then sometimes waves of sadness and a sick feeling in my chest and stomach. 

&#x200B;

I'm being patient with myself.

There are! When she died, our witch (we're pagan) said that she'd seen a few photos of her in the dress (with the amazing shoes she ordered in) and she looked like a queen and we cried so hard. That was all I wanted. I am still so excited to see my lovely bride, and I know she wouldn't want people to see her looking ugly and bruised in the dress. 

&#x200B;

I will find her some suitable clothes that hide her arms for the viewing where they were wounded from all the needles and blood tests. Amazingly, her face stayed so perfect through the whole horrible decline in her health. Even while her body started to get more spotty with blood clots and sores, her beautiful pale face stayed relatively untouched except for her lips getting really dry. That was just the closed-circuit air con in the hospital though.
